---
args: { input: CaseInput }
returns: RunProposal
---
1. Bind `goal = await frameRequest(input)` from the request and `policy = await selectPolicy(input)` from supplied authority candidates. Preserve unresolved precedence instead of guessing which source governs.
2. Bind `work = await formTaskGraph(goal)` and `evidencePlan = await planEvidence(input, work)` so each operation has explicit prerequisites and a searched source universe.
3. Run the stages in their dependency order. The first stage receives only `input.domainRecords.firstStage`; every later stage receives the preceding function's actual accepted records. Bind each full result separately.
const interpretObservationsResult = await interpretObservations(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan);
const selectProcedureResult = await selectProcedure(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, interpretObservationsResult.accepted);
const constructWorkPlanResult = await constructWorkPlan(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, selectProcedureResult.accepted);
const interpretProgressResult = await interpretProgress(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, constructWorkPlanResult.accepted);
const composeHandoverResult = await composeHandover(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, interpretProgressResult.accepted);
4. Bind `stageSet: CaseStageSet = { interpretObservations: interpretObservationsResult, selectProcedure: selectProcedureResult, constructWorkPlan: constructWorkPlanResult, interpretProgress: interpretProgressResult, composeHandover: composeHandoverResult }` and `collection: CollectionFinding = await reconcileCollection(stageSet)`. Bind `allQuestions: string[] = [...interpretObservationsResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...selectProcedureResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...constructWorkPlanResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...interpretProgressResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...composeHandoverResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...collection.coverageGaps]` and `questions: QuestionBatch = await resolveQuestions(allQuestions, input)`.
5. Bind `invalidation = await assessDelta(input)`, `review = await prepareReview(collection)`, and `view = await composeView(review, input)`; pass each child its actual declared inputs and retain the returned object.
6. Bind `allChecks: CheckResult[] = [...interpretObservationsResult.checks, ...selectProcedureResult.checks, ...constructWorkPlanResult.checks, ...interpretProgressResult.checks, ...composeHandoverResult.checks]`. Bind `hasGateFailure = allChecks.some(check => check.verdict !== "pass")` and `hasBlocker = input.authorityStatus !== "authorized" || questions.questions.length > 0 || collection.coverageGaps.length > 0`. Bind `disposition: "proposed" | "blocked" | "needs-review" = hasBlocker ? "blocked" : hasGateFailure ? "needs-review" : "proposed"`. Bind `rationale: string[] = allChecks.map(check => `${check.check}: ${check.verdict}; evidence ${check.evidenceIds.join(",")}`)`.
7. Operational detail 1 — A technician reports done but the verification is missing: keep the task incomplete. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (keep the task incomplete.) through the existing stage result for AssetObservation; preserve exact source/version and the prior AssetObservation, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
8. Operational detail 2 — A spare part has a different revision: require compatibility review before installation. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (require compatibility review before installation.) through the existing stage result for AssetObservation; preserve exact source/version and the prior AssetObservation, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
9. Operational detail 3 — A shift ends during isolation: carry the exact state and required checks into handover. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (carry the exact state and required checks into handover.) through the existing stage result for AssetObservation; preserve exact source/version and the prior AssetObservation, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
10. Operational detail 4 — A recurring fault disappears temporarily: retain its history and approved monitoring requirement. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (retain its history and approved monitoring requirement.) through the existing stage result for AssetObservation; preserve exact source/version and the prior AssetObservation, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
11. Operational detail 5 — An asset identifier is ambiguous: verify identity before dispatching work. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (verify identity before dispatching work.) through the existing stage result for AssetObservation; preserve exact source/version and the prior AssetObservation, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
12. Initialize `revisions: RevisionProposal[] = []`. If any gate is not pass, bind `revision = await proposeRevision(the failed check names, the smallest affected stage name)` and add that returned proposal to revisions. Bind and return `result: RunProposal = { caseId: input.caseId, goal, policy, work, evidencePlan, interpretObservations: interpretObservationsResult, selectProcedure: selectProcedureResult, constructWorkPlan: constructWorkPlanResult, interpretProgress: interpretProgressResult, composeHandover: composeHandoverResult, collection, questions, invalidation, review, view, revisions, disposition, rationale }`. Proposed actions remain proposals. The host owns authorization, persistence, effect dispatch and verification.
